.TH PCAP-CONFIG 1 "May 22, 2009"
.SH NAME
pcap-config \- write libpcap compiler and linker flags to standard output
.SH SYNOPSIS
.na
.B pcap-config
[
.B \-\-static
]
[
.B \-\-cflags
]
[
.B \-\-libs | \-\-additional-libs
]
.ad
.SH DESCRIPTION
When run with the
.B \-\-cflags
option,
.I pcap-config
writes to the standard output the
.B \-I
compiler flags required to include libpcap's header files.
When run with the
.B \-\-libs
option,
.I pcap-config
writes to the standard output the
.B \-L
and
.B \-l
linker flags required to link with libpcap. For shared linking, these
may also include a run-time search path. For static linking, they
include the additional libraries required by libpcap.
When run with the
.B \-\-additional-libs
option,
.I pcap-config
reports only the additional linker flags for libpcap's dependencies.
There are no such flags for shared linking; with
.B \-\-static
these are the dependency flags recorded at configure time, without
the search path or link flag for libpcap itself.
.LP
By default, it writes flags for linking with the shared libpcap library. The
.B \-\-static
option reports the flags needed when linking with the archive; it does
not force the linker to select that archive.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
pcap(3PCAP)
